# APEX Trading Terminal — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
APEX is an AI-powered trading terminal (Bloomberg-style) using Claude AI agents, Supabase Realtime, and Vercel.
- **Repo**: https://github.com/adnanmoffice-bt/trader1
- **Master Log**: Always read `APEX_PROJECT_LOG.md` before any major change.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 15.1.0 + React 19 + TypeScript 5.6 (strict mode)
- Tailwind CSS 3.4 with custom dark theme
- Supabase (PostgreSQL + Realtime + RLS)
- Anthropic Claude Sonnet 4 (`claude-sonnet-4-20250514`)
- Zustand 5.0 for state management
- Vercel for hosting + cron jobs
- Telegram Bot for notifications

## Path Aliases
- `@/*` maps to project root (tsconfig paths)
- Example: `import { useStore } from '@/lib/store'`

## File Organization
- Types: `types/index.ts` — ALL interfaces live here, never scatter types
- Agents: `agents/index.ts` — ALL 5 agents in one file
- Lib: `lib/` — utility modules (anthropic, indicators, price-fetcher, store, supabase, telegram)
- API: `app/api/` — Next.js route handlers
- Cron: `app/api/cron/` — Vercel cron endpoints (require `Bearer CRON_SECRET`)
- Components: `components/` — React components
- Schema: `supabase/schema.sql` — complete DB schema

## Coding Rules

### TypeScript
- Strict mode — no `any` types unless absolutely necessary
- All interfaces in `types/index.ts`
- Use `import type` for type-only imports
- Prefer `const` functions with explicit return types for exports

### React / Next.js
- `'use client'` directive required for client components
- Server Components by default
- API routes use `NextRequest`/`NextResponse`
- Dashboard uses route groups: `app/(dashboard)/page.tsx`

### Supabase
- Browser client: `createBrowserSupabase()` or `getBrowserSupabase()` (singleton)
- Server/API client: `createServiceSupabase()` — NEVER use anon key server-side
- All DB writes go through service role client
- RLS is enabled on ALL tables

### AI Agents
- All agents called via `callAgent<T>()` from `lib/anthropic.ts`
- `expectJson: true` strips code fences and parses JSON
- Signal confidence threshold: 65% minimum
- Risk-reward minimum: 1.5x
- Max open positions: 3
- Max risk per trade: 5% of capital

### Styling
- Bloomberg terminal dark theme
- Background: `#03030a` (void), `#07070f` (deep), `#0b0b16` (base)
- Green: `#00ffa3` (profit/bullish)
- Red: `#ff3366` (loss/bearish)
- Amber: `#ffcc00` (neutral/warning)
- Cyan: `#00ccff` (info)
- Purple: `#9966ff` (AI/agent)
- Fonts: Inter (sans), JetBrains Mono (mono)
- Use `.mono` class for financial numbers

### UI Language
- Dashboard UI text is in Bosnian/Croatian (Prilike, Vijesti, Agenti, Pozicije, Kapital)
- Technical labels and API responses stay in English

### Currency & Numbers
- Primary currency: AED (UAE Dirham)
- AED/USD rate: 3.6725
- Always show financial numbers with `toLocaleString('en')` or `.toFixed(2)`
- Prefix prices with `$`, P&L with `AED`

## Environment Variables
- NEVER hardcode API keys
- All keys documented in `.env.example`
- 13 integrations total (see APEX_PROJECT_LOG.md section 7)

## Database Tables (10)
market_data, signals, trades, positions, portfolio, news, agent_logs, price_history, demo_sessions, demo_trades

## Cron Jobs
- `/api/cron/market-data` — every 1 min
- `/api/cron/signals` — every 30 min
- `/api/cron/positions` — every 2 min (TODO: create endpoint)
- `/api/cron/demo` — every 15 min (TODO: create endpoint)

## Before Making Changes
1. Read `APEX_PROJECT_LOG.md` for full project context
2. Check `types/index.ts` for existing interfaces
3. Update the changelog section in `APEX_PROJECT_LOG.md` after significant changes
4. Run `npm run build` to verify no TypeScript errors
5. Never commit `.env.local` or any PEM files
